  "body": "Non-fetch scheme navigation params's initiator origin is populated in two places:\r\n - https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#populating-a-session-history-entry:non-fetch-scheme-params-initiator-origin, in #attempt-to-populate, where we explicitly navigate to a non-fetch scheme URL\r\n - https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#populating-a-session-history-entry:non-fetch-scheme-params-initiator-origin-2 in #create-navigation-params-by-fetching, when we redirect to a non-fetch scheme URL\r\n\r\nThe second instance above is setting the initiator origin to something completely bogus — the \"origin\" concept, not even a variable. I think this should instead be _responseOrigin_, to be the last fetch-scheme origin in the redirect chain, but need to take a closer look.",
